Or be me, and leave them littered about on the floor because I'm too lazy
to pick them up.

I pick up scrolls, wands, potions...I check armor if it's convenient
(yeah, I probably miss out on some +4 helms that way...but I don't die of
bordom, either :-)  ), and weapons?  Unless it's an artifact weapon, I
generally don't even bother picking it up.  Exception is missle weapons -
I'll often pick up enough daggers to use, and then just dodge the ones
lying around on the floor that monsters pick up and throw at me.  If I'm
being good, I'll pick up arrows, too - they're light, and it's easy enough
to keep them out of monsters' hands.  Finally, I almost *always* pick up
poisoned weapons - don't want any of *those* flying around, even if *I*'m
resistant - Fluffy isn't.

Eventually, find a box and stash stuff :-)

I like a box/chest on the level with the mines branch, if that's feasible.

Good luck, and remember, it's better to leave junk on the floor then it is
to be burdoned!!  You can always run away from an orc carrying a scimitar,
but he can kill you barehanded if you're burdoned...

